<article class="env-definition" id="04CT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04CT">Definition <span data-tag="04CT">76.7.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. The <em>sheaf of differentials $\Omega _{X/Y}$ of $X$ over $Y$</em> is sheaf of differentials (Modules on Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/04BQ" data-tag="04BQ">18.33.10</a>) for the morphism of ringed topoi </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (f_{small}, f^\sharp ) : (X_{\acute{e}tale}, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \mathcal{O}_ Y)  \]
</div>
  <p> of Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03G8" data-tag="03G8">66.21.3</a>. The <em>universal $Y$-derivation</em> will be denoted $\text{d}_{X/Y} : \mathcal{O}_ X \to \Omega _{X/Y}$. </p>
</article>